  "final": "I implemented the PATCH contract in `src/parser.ts` and `src/service.ts`. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes. I didn't add any new checks, so the new validation rules are untested beyond the existing public check.\n\n**`parseProfile` in `src/parser.ts`:**\n- **Input shape:** it rejects non-objects, `null`, arrays, and any prototype other than `Object.prototype` or `null`. Any own key other than `displayName` or `tags` is rejected too, including symbol keys.\n- **`displayName`:**\n  - An absent key keeps the stored value.\n  - `null` clears it.\n  - A string is trimmed and must be 1 to 40 characters long.\n  - Any other value is invalid, including `undefined` and numbers.\n- **`tags`:**\n  - An absent key keeps the stored tags.\n  - `null` or `[]` clears them.\n  - An array may hold at most 5 items. Each must be a string, with no holes and no coercion.\n  - Each tag is trimmed first, then must be 1 to 12 characters long and distinct from the others.\n  - The parser builds a new array rather than reusing the caller's.\n- **Errors:** every failure throws `Error('invalid profile')`.\n\n**`ProfileService.patch` in `src/service.ts`:**\n- It parses before it changes anything, so an invalid input leaves storage unchanged.\n- An empty object is a no-op.\n- It stores a copy of the tags array.\n- It returns the stored profile, as before, so the public interface is unchanged.\n\nThe input object is only read, never modified.",
